      "text": "To solve the system of linear equations given by \\[\n\\begin{align*}\n3x - 5y &= -11, \\\\\n7x + 2y &= -12,\n\\end{align*}\n\\] we can use the method of elimination. \n\nFirst, we'll eliminate \\(y\\) by making the coefficients of \\(y\\) in both equations equal in magnitude but opposite in sign. To achieve this, we can multiply the first equation by 2 and the second equation by 5:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n2(3x - 5y) &= 2(-11), \\\\\n5(7x + 2y) &= 5(-12).\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThis results in:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n6x - 10y &= -22, \\\\\n35x + 10y &= -60.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nNext, we add these two equations together to eliminate \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\n(6x - 10y) + (35x + 10y) = -22 + (-60).\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n41x = -82.\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-82}{41} = -2.\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(x = -2\\), we substitute it back into one of the original equations to solve for \\(y\\). Let's use the first equation:\n\n\\[\n3(-2) - 5y = -11.\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n-6 - 5y = -11.\n\\]\n\nWe solve for \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\n-5y = -11 + 6,\n\\]\n\\[\n-5y = -5,\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 1.\n\\]\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is:\n\n\\[\n(x, y) = (-2, 1).\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this solution by substituting \\(x = -2\\) and \\(y = 1\\) back into the original equations.\n\nFinal answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(-2, 1)}\n\\]\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the variables\r\nx, y = symbols('x y')\r\n\r\n# Define the equations\r\neq1 = Eq(3*x - 5*y, -11)\r\neq2 = Eq(7*x + 2*y, -12)\r\n\r\n# Solve the system of equations\r\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2), (x, y))\r\nprint(solution)\n```",
